\begin{align*}(\sqrt{45+(d^{2}+6d+9)})^{2} &= 9d^{2} \end{align*}

From here, we find: \begin{align*}54+d^2+6d &= 9d^2 \end{align*}

This gives us the quadratic equation: \begin{align*}8d^{2}-6d-54 &= 0 \end{align*}

From here, we use the quadratic formula to find our $d$s: \begin{align*} d&=\frac{-(-6)±\sqrt{(-6)^{2}-4(8)(-54)}}{16}\\&=\frac{6±\sqrt{2070}}{16}\\ &=\frac{6±10\sqrt{21}}{16}\\ &=\frac{3±5\sqrt{21}}{8} \end{align*}

We get two possible answers for $d$: $\frac{ 3+5\sqrt{21} }{8}$ and $\frac{ 3-5\sqrt{21} }{8}$

The question says "smallest possible value", so we go with $\frac{ 3-5\sqrt{21} }{8}$

